ree cash flow.","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is 63%.","ROE of 10% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.7x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 12pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.4% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 4.4x net debt to EBITDA ($608.0M of cash against $16.8B of debt), with interest covered 4.3x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.32 in the distress zone."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 15.5% over 3 years and 26.7% over 5 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 119%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 23.3% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.8% trend).","Forward indicators: FFO growth of 23.2% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.4x depreciation (0.0% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and institutions hold 97%.","It returns 5.4% a year to shareholders (7.4% in dividends, less 1.4% of net share issuance).","The share count has grown 11.9% a year over five years, diluting existing holders."],"people":["With about 28 employees, each generates about $143.1M of revenue, 62.7x the Real Estate median, and revenue has grown 46.6% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $89.6M of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $5.5M (0x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $578K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":78,"head":"Invest: trades 48% below fair value of $47.72; FCF margin 62.6%.","pros":["Composite 49, above the 39 line (gates 14/25)","Trades 48% below fair value of $47.72","FCF margin 62.6%","Revenue grew 26.7%/yr over 5y","P/E 11.6x